      "content": "fair enough. let's focus on the general arguments then. when you look at the arguments against these types of voting legislation—like the ones about \"election integrity\" or \"preventing fraud\"—how do they stack up against the claims of \"voter suppression\"? are the integrity concerns actually backed by data, or do they tend to be viewed as just a way to justify restrictive laws?",
